title: Questions
tags: Contents

!!! Does it cost anything?

The editor is free. Pinning is done by the service or node you choose: your own node costs nothing more, and services such as Filebase and Pinata have free plans of their own.

!!! Who owns a wiki?

The people who hold the key of its address. Anyone may publish a version of any wiki, at an address of their own, but only the holder of an address's key decides which version the address shows. The owner of an ENS name decides which address the name points to.

!!! Can I delete a published version?

You can unpin it from the services you used. A version stays reachable for as long as any node keeps it, so treat publishing as permanent. Publishing a newer version changes what the wiki's address shows, but the older version stays at its own IPFS address.

!!! How long does a wiki's address stay up?

Orivon's node keeps it up for 30 days after each publish. The record is valid for ten years, so you or anyone holding the public record file can republish it with any IPFS node. See [[A wiki's address]].

!!! What if I lose the key of an address?

Nobody can update that address again. Publish the wiki under a new address and point your ENS name at it. Download the key when the editor offers it, and again from ''Settings'' whenever you need a copy.

!!! Can I update a wiki from another browser?

Yes: import the key of its address in the other browser, and the wiki from its address or from a backup. The editor then offers to update the address.

!!! Does it work outside Orivon?

Yes. In other browsers a wiki opens through an IPFS gateway, such as `yourname.eth.limo`, and the pen opens the editor at `editor.decentrawiki.eth.limo`. Orivon opens both at their own names and checks every file of them against their addresses.

!!! Can I use my own TiddlyWiki plugins?

Yes. A wiki's plugins come across when it is imported and are published with it. Only the DecentraWiki plugin is the editor's own, so the pen on every published wiki works the same way.